   418	## Integrate reports deliberately
   419	
   420	- Keep the model and its fixed reference files together, and treat malformed
   421	  input separately from a failed domain rule.
   422	- Branch on documented fields and `schema_version`. Reference and temporal
   423	  features select report variants; do not assume one version for all models.
   424	- Model-based redaction applies by default to checking, verbalization, and
   425	  diff reports. `unredacted=True` is an explicit request to retain source
   426	  values. Under the [disclosure mode](disclosure.md) `internal` it is granted
   427	  without asking; under `customer` it raises `DisclosureRefused`.
   428	- Wrong Python argument types can raise `TypeError` before evaluation. Returned
   429	  report failures are not a substitute for ordinary exception handling.
   430	- A mechanical pass checks supplied facts against supplied rules. Assurance
   431	  metadata is a separate result; missing or stale evidence remains unavailable.
   432	
   433	The current signatures live in
   434	[the public API module](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/blob/main/src/gnd/api.py).
   435	The [format index](formats.md) points to the authoritative contracts for each
   436	report and input family.
   437	
   438	### Compiled snapshot operation obligations
   439	
   440	`api.check(model, population, compiled_operations=True)` adds eligible standing
   441	operation subsets to a snapshot check. Default checking still excludes operations.
   442	Known alethic violations appear as `compiled-subset` verdicts and band 1; missing
   443	coverage/unknown inputs appear as unchecked. Reports carry no proof-backed
   444	assurance for this new mode. `admission=True` cannot be combined with it. Use
   445	`api.transition` for step, dynamic, intermediate-state and frame obligations.
   446	
   447	## Reusing a checked pre-state
   448	
   449	`check_with_receipt(model, population, *, unredacted=False)` accepts loaded objects
   450	and returns `(payload, receipt)`. The payload is the same as `check` produces.
   451	Pass the receipt as `transition(..., pre_receipt=receipt)` to skip the pre-state
   452	check. Intermediate and post checks still run.
   453	
   454	The `CheckReceipt` docstring defines the receipt contract. GND alone mints these
   455	opaque values. Reuse binds the same model object and unchanged model content,
   456	a validated population with the same content, the stored report and branch ids,
   457	and default check options. Exit 0 or 2 can be reused; anchored models and models
   458	without a cacheable key cannot.
   459	
   460	Invalid reuse raises `ReceiptRefused`, a `ValueError` with a `reason` attribute.
   461	The first failing guard wins, in this order:
   462	
   463	| Reason | Meaning |
   464	|---|---|
   465	| `foreign` | GND did not mint this receipt |
   466	| `path-inputs` | Model or pre-state is a path |
   467	| `not-reusable` | The check failed or its route cannot be reused |
   468	| `options` | References or different check options were requested |
   469	| `model-object` | A different model object was supplied |
   470	| `model-changed` | Model content changed, including operations |
   471	| `population-unvalidated` | The pre-state lacks a current validation marker |
   472	| `population-changed` | Validated pre-state content differs from the receipt |
   473	
   474	Receipts stay in one process and cannot be serialized. There is no CLI option.
   475	Only default check options are supported; compiled operations, admission,
   476	anchors and references are outside this feature.
   477	
   478	
   479	## Reusing evaluation work across snapshots
   480	
   481	`EvaluationSession(model, *, max_rows=100000, max_bytes=33554432)` takes a loaded
   482	`Model`. Load every population with that same model. `session.check(population)`
   483	and `session.transition(pre, steps, post=None)` return the ordinary API payloads;
   484	`session.check_with_receipt(population)` returns the ordinary payload/receipt pair.
   485	The normal stateless functions, CLI, batch and experiment defaults remain fresh.
   486	
   487	The session rechecks current validation markers, model content including operations,
   488	ordered facts, rosters, coverage and supported options. A no-op can reuse eligible
   489	extension components and constraint findings. A change recomputes the dirty
   490	component from current inputs, including whole recursive components; it preserves
   491	current witnesses, lineage, unavailable/possible states, branch evidence and report
   492	ordering. Admission and every required root/intermediate/post check still run.
   493	Snapshot comparison remains proportional to input size. This is component reuse,
   494	not a promise of work proportional only to added rows.
   495	
   496	Reference, anchored, witness/observer, compiled/admission and unknown dependency
   497	modes select fresh work as applicable. Custom family hooks with unclassified
   498	external dependencies also run fresh. Unsupported keys or resource bounds never
   499	substitute an empty relation for unavailable data. `check` accepts the normal
   500	semantic keywords; `transition` accepts `unredacted`, `references` and `pre_receipt`.
   501	Results are detached from stored findings. A receipt's mutable public report also
   502	cannot change the private snapshot later consumed by a transition.
   503	
   504	A session retains one committed generation, up to the configured projected bytes
   505	and retained fact/witness rows. Oversized/unmeasurable units run fresh. The byte
   506	projection bounds cache content, not Python RSS or caller-owned inputs. A completed
   507	violation can publish valid units; errors/indeterminate checks discard staged cache
   508	work. Exceptions/cancellation before publication preserve committed cache and
   509	feedback sequence. One active call per session is permitted; overlapping calls
   510	raise `ValueError`. Independent sessions may interleave. `reset()` clears retained
   511	work; `close()` releases it and rejects future work. Sessions cannot be serialized.
   512	
   513	`stats()` is diagnostic and stays outside reports/feedback. `lookups` counts each owned unit lookup once. `hits`, `misses` and
   514	`bypasses` are overlapping event counters: a computed miss may also bypass storage
   515	because of a bound. Their sum is not a lookup denominator; use `bypasses/lookups`
   516	for that fraction. A zero denominator means no rate was measured. `session_calls`/`session_fresh_calls` count
   517	completed or attempted facade evaluations under ownership; `extension_context_calls`
